{"title":"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/68269b799b7a534ce3266d4e3c8b73e83f13cb70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|x+y\\right|+\\left|x-y\\right|=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />. What is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/4/f74bdc11951db06cc5c7ee7c520c297376c8c28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-6x+y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebccb94c356d4c6a364d75aad166d4749fcd39ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Plugging in some values, we see that the  graph of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bf6183c2f00385b53a1e9ddbe0b55e90afddb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x+y|+|x-y| = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> is a square bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2cb78b31c6eea2ef509984603219a91867935af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/6601418f5acf74318228ed02eb2b99dc8c4db6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18c8242033e22ade3df383cd774708693552b877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 6x + y^2 = (x-3)^2 + y^2 - 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"256\" height=\"19\" /> means the square of the distance from a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af424ab2c41e93a9e7ab081dee423809b2ba735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> minus 9. To maximize that value, we need to choose the point in the feasible region farthest from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af424ab2c41e93a9e7ab081dee423809b2ba735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe78b99fa2c727dd05f5486e73a376b2e83ce31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, \\pm 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />. Either one, when substituting into the function, yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114228a01e21efe5394aa489ccef5bb000ccd93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bf6183c2f00385b53a1e9ddbe0b55e90afddb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x+y|+|x-y| = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> is dealing with absolute values, the following could be deduced: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4cdee9e38ea584231849ed1165c61ac7556b513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y)+(x-y)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d69b423ce871a06d506a045cfba26dd48a93fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y)-(x-y)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84d8d143d7f20a569926f513f6bf077a89347f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(x+y)+(x-y)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17eaeb4df713d75a1a56aa362c8a12447b996878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(x+y)-(x-y)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />. Simplifying would give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbab939b716843df7cc6fdb3e9a0b91b2fea5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c2e8c17cff668023b2f29f2e95e4a0fafa6271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/4/f74bdc11951db06cc5c7ee7c520c297376c8c28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-6x+y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, we care most about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/1009021fa18e2843323bab9ed4b345dda018cf89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a3faa3658bcbd8bde8e16cfa5baf019619fc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> are non-negative. To maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b6790c9ffc33aa66a7e235079d5619d3ed77236d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6x$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, though, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> would have to be -1. Therefore, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c2e8c17cff668023b2f29f2e95e4a0fafa6271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbab939b716843df7cc6fdb3e9a0b91b2fea5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, the equation evaluates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114228a01e21efe5394aa489ccef5bb000ccd93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A\">2011 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /